alex: Weird one in the Node sampleapp: when token refresh kicks in the x-request-id disappears from downstream logs. tracing gets broken. :frowning:

tina_infra: Repro steps? staging only?

alex: staging. call /user/profile with expired token -> auth middleware does refresh -> it retries the original request. initial request shows x-request-id, retry does not.

jamal_sdk: Likely propagation + retry ordering. Are we installing otel propagator before the app logging hook?

alex: we do `app.use(otelMiddleware)` then `app.use(reqLogger)` but the retry is done by axios-retry inside the auth middleware. looks like axios-retry issues a new request w/o copying inbound headers.

jamal_sdk: Short fix: add an axios request interceptor that injects x-request-id into outgoing requests from context. Example:
```js
axios.interceptors.request.use(cfg => {
  const id = reqContext.get('x-request-id');
  if (id) cfg.headers['x-request-id'] = id;
  return cfg;
});
```

alex: that fixed the propagation locally, thanks. but we then hit a redaction bug: our header-redactor strips Authorization but collapses header map and sometimes drops x-request-id when redacting. filed bug #DX-428.

tina_infra: So two things: 1) make retry-aware propagation part of sampleapp template; 2) change redactor to operate key-by-key and preserve non-sensitive headers.

